  {% set bytesimPrimary = providerB.codes | findCode(providerB.primaryCode) %}

  <div class="content-callout">
    <h2>The Short Answer</h2>
    <p>
      Both SimLocal and ByteSIM are rare on this site for selling a real phone number, not just data. Pick <strong>SimLocal</strong> if your trip is to the UK and you want that number bundled into the plan for free with no ID check. Pick <strong>ByteSIM</strong> if you need a number somewhere else, since it covers nine countries including the UK, US, Canada, France, Spain, Australia, Vietnam, South Korea, and Thailand, at the cost of a passport-and-selfie verification step.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>The Core Difference: Free and Bundled vs. Verified and Wider</h2>
  <p>
    SimLocal's UK plans fold a full UK phone number straight into the plan: no separate product, no ID upload, no extra step. We bought one ourselves for a UK trip specifically for this reason and confirmed it works for calls and texts, not just data. The catch is that it's UK-only; SimLocal doesn't sell a bundled number for any other country.
  </p>
  <p>
    ByteSIM takes the opposite approach: a real number is a specific plan you choose, available in nine countries, with identity verification required by local telecom regulation (a passport photo and a selfie) before the number activates. That's more friction than SimLocal's UK number, but it's also the only one of the two that can give you a US, Canadian, or Southeast Asian number, not just a British one.
  </p>

  <h2>Feature Snapshot</h2>
